SUMMARY:Implementing Zero Trust Security Architectures: Federated vs Centr
 alized
DESCRIPTION:Cloud Data Driven\n🔐 **Securing modern data systems** is no
  longer about boundaries - it is about trust\, identity\, and control.\n\n
 As enterprise data ecosystems expand across hybrid and multi-cloud environ
 ments\, traditional perimeter-based security models are no longer sufficie
 nt to protect sensitive information. Organizations are increasingly adopti
 ng Zero Trust Architecture (ZTA) to secure complex data environments where
  information flows across distributed platforms\, services\, and organizat
 ional boundaries.\n\n💡 **In this session**\, we explore how Zero Trust 
 principles can be applied to modern enterprise data architectures\, focusi
 ng on the security implications of federated and centralized data models.\
 n\n🔍 **What will be covered:**\n\n🔹 How federated and centralized ar
 chitectures handle identity management\n🔹 Approaches to access control 
 in distributed environments\n🔹 Data governance strategies within a Zero
  Trust framework\n\n⚖️ **Architectural trade-offs:**\n\n🔹 Federated
  architectures support data sovereignty\, localized policy enforcement\, a
 nd distributed resilience\n🔹 Centralized architectures enable unified s
 ecurity policies\, centralized monitoring\, and coordinated threat respons
 e\n\n**🤖 AI and Zero Trust:**\n\n🔹 Real-time threat detection powere
 d by AI\n🔹 Behavioral analytics for anomaly identification\n🔹 Automa
 ted response mechanisms to mitigate risks\n\n**🛡️ Protecting modern d
 ata pipelines:**\n\n🔹 Securing AI-powered data pipelines end-to-end\n
 🔹 Maintaining data lineage visibility across systems\n🔹 Ensuring com
 pliance with evolving regulatory requirements\n\n**🎯 Learning objective
 s:**\n\n🔹 Design secure and scalable enterprise data systems\n🔹 Unde
 rstand the trade-offs between federated and centralized models\n🔹 Imple
 ment Zero Trust strategies for stronger data protection in AI-enabled envi
 ronments\n\n**📊 Level:** Intermediate\n\n**📅 Date/Time:** Thursday\,
  Apr 30 · 12:00 PM EST\n\n🎤 **Speaker:** Vineel Bala - Director\, Data
 base Administration at Fidelity Investments. Contact: 👉 https://www.lin
 kedin.com/in/vineel-bala-434250101/\n\n🎙 **Moderator:** Ronen Ariely \\
 - 🌐 Sr\\. Consultant & Data Architect \\| 🎤 Intl\\. Speaker & Lectur
 er \\| 🏆 7x Former MVP \\| 🌍 Lead: Data Driven Community & GlobalHeb
 rew \\| 💾 Data Platforms Expert\\. Contact: 👉 https://www\\.linkedin
 \\.com/in/pitoach/ 👉 https://www\\.facebook\\.com/ronen\\.ariely\n\n▬
 ▬▬▬▬ **About the community** ▬▬▬▬▬\n*📌Data Driven Com
 munity & Cloud Data-Driven user group*\n*The Cloud Data-Driven User Group 
 is the official user group of the Data-Driven Community\, hosting weekly m
 eetings as part of our community-driven activities. For a full list of upc
 oming events and more details about our community\, visit: [https://datadr
 ivencommunity.com](https://datadrivencommunity.com)*\n▬▬▬▬▬▬
 ▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬
